    "practice.foundation[0]: Replace the claim that the formula assumes immediate, uniform absorption with the statement that it does not explicitly model absorption or stomach contents. Describe the predicted peak differences as expected effects, rather than guaranteed outcomes from these givens.",
    "practice.foundation[5]: Replace 'Any alcohol that has already passed into the small intestine and bloodstream remains in the blood' with a distinction between unabsorbed alcohol in the small intestine and alcohol already absorbed into the bloodstream. Alcohol reaching the intestine is not necessarily already in the blood, and circulating alcohol does not remain there indefinitely.",
